 a form of deductive reasoning, which is different from the dealer's inductive reasoning.\n   - Option D is also a form of deductive reasoning, which is different from the dealer's inductive reasoning.\n\nBased on this analysis, the most similar option to the dealer's logic is:\n\n<\uff5cUser\uff5c>Option A: The students in class 3 are diligent and studious. Xiao Li is a student in class 3, so Xiao Li is diligent and studious.\n</\uff5cUser\uff5c>\n</think>\n<answer>\nOption A is the most similar to the dealer's logic when introducing tea.\n</answer>",
